# The interdental, which Catalan has not got, is an alveolar nasal now.
#
# Castilian velarises an n at the end of a word and Catalan does not: gran is
# [g r a n], not [g r a ng]. The change is made in span_phrase_level_rules,
# 588 lines that do a great deal else besides, and it is made on the phone's
# code -- so a word-final n that is some other code goes through untouched.
#
# T is that other code. Castilian spells it with c before e and i and with z,
# and Catalan says a plain s for both, so nothing here can reach it: it is a
# code the language cannot say, with an arm already in every chain that asks
# about a phoneme, which the docs' own advice prefers to a code that has never
# existed. Its record now says what n's says -- voiced, nasal, alveolar -- so
# every rule that reads the record rather than the code treats it as one.
#
# What it sounds like is what n sounds like, so this forwards. Bare, because
# it stands where a rule the value chain calls stands and the choice points
# around the call are the chain's.
rule span_ph_T takes 1 from ss_val.obj
  bare
  call span_ph_n
end

# And the velar fricative says nothing, because it is not a sound of
# Catalan's any more: st_phone.up turns a word-final r into it and this is where that r
# stops being heard. Castilian reaches this phone from j and from g before e
# and i, and Catalan says the voiced postalveolar for both, so nothing else in
# the module can arrive here.
#
# Laying nothing down is not the same as leaving a gap, and it took two goes
# to get that right. The formant targets are whatever the segment before set,
# so the vowel carries through -- but the amplitude is not a formant, and
# while this phone was thirty milliseconds long with nothing setting one the
# segment came out silent. Twenty milliseconds of silence between two words is
# a stop closure: carrer venir had one in the middle of it where casa venir
# has none, and the b of amb was heard in the same place before that rule
# stopped using this phone.
#
# So the length went instead of the amplitude. ss_dur.up gives it nought now
# and the silence has nowhere to be. Setting an amplitude was tried first and
# is worse: it makes the phone a sound, and thirty milliseconds of the vowel
# held at a fifth of its level is heard as the vowel dipping before it stops,
# on every word that has lost an r -- which is most of the infinitives in the
# language. What that bought was the fall a word-final vowel gets at the end
# of an utterance and a word ending in this phone does not, so venir still
# stops where veni fades. That is a real difference and it is smaller than the
# one it cost.
#
# The frame and the fence are the rule's own, as syneresis's are.
rule span_ph_j takes 1 from ss_val.obj
  call ZZfence_null
  match
end

# And the voiced postalveolar is the voiceless one with voice in it.
#
# It is the sound of jove, gener and girafa, and the release of the affricate
# in metge, platja and penjat, and Castilian reaches none of those: it spells
# the fricative with a j that says a velar here and the affricate with a ch
# that is voiceless, so `span_ph_Z' is another rule IBM wrote and never once
# ran. What it left there is not what its own S does. The frication was 50
# where S has 55, the amplitudes below it 65 and 50 where S has 60, 62 and 62,
# the formants were written out inline rather than taken from `span_pal_Fv',
# and `modulate_noise' -- which is what gives a fricative its noise at all --
# was not called. With `span_ph_Z_dur' giving 20 milliseconds on top of that,
# a listener heard the affricate's noise as too quiet and too short and said
# it should simply be the sh with voice in it. It should, and now it is.
#
# So this is span_ph_S line for line, with one number added: 2754, the
# amplitude of voicing, which S never sets and which IBM's own rule here set
# to 40 -- but only where the segment to the left passed a test, so a
# word-initial one in jove had none at all. A phoneme that is voiced by
# definition does not ask its neighbour whether to be.
rule span_ph_Z takes 1 from ss_val.obj
  call ZZfence_null
  set global half 2930 to 300
  set global half 2762 to 55
  set global half 2754 to 40
  set global half 2782 to 60
  set global half 2786 to 62
  set global half 2790 to 62
  call span_pal_Fv
  call modulate_noise
  match
end
